<title>UK: Parmalat prices $150 mln Jan 2005 bond, put, call.</title>
<headline>Parmalat prices $150 mln Jan 2005 bond, put, call.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced by lead manager Bank of Boston.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PARMALAT BRAZIL</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	COUPON  ** 9.125     MATURITY  * 02.JAN.05</p>
<p> TYPE   STEP-UP	 ISS PRICE  99.922    PAY DATE  S-06.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    99.922    S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 SPREAD	300 BP</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    =	   CRS DEFLT  =	   FORCE MAJ   =</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p> NOTES    * PUT AND CALL AT PAR ON 02.JAN.00</p>
<p>	   ** STEPS UP TO 9.75 PCT AFTER YEAR THREE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
